  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">Why the sector matters less than the records</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Two companies in the same sector can get different answers. The question a buyer asks is what the records actually show, and whether your company holds the right to license them &mdash; not which industry you are in.</p>
      <p class="reveal">A manufacturer&rsquo;s maintenance log and a law firm&rsquo;s matter file raise different contract questions, but both are only usable if the work is written down and still sits in the system that produced it. The sector tells us which questions to ask first. It does not decide the answer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

